@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "About";
}

<div class="about-container" style="max-width: 1000px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 3rem 1rem;">
    
    <div style="text-align: center; margin-bottom: 3rem;">
        <!-- FIX: Updated to cyan with a burnt orange underline -->
        <h1 style="color: var(--cyan-bright); border-bottom: 4px solid var(--burnt-orange); display: inline-block; padding-bottom: 0.5rem;">
            The Builder Behind the Code
        </h1>
    </div>

    <!-- Flex container for image and text -->
    <div style="display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 3rem; align-items: flex-start;">
        
        <!-- Left Column: Professional Headshot -->
        <div style="flex: 1 1 300px; text-align: center;">
            <img src="~/images/main-logo.png" 
                 alt="Zac Kimball - Zues Digital Designs" 
                 style="width: 100%; max-width: 400px; border-radius: 8px; border-bottom: 5px solid var(--electric-blue); box-shadow: 0 4px 15px rgba(19, 160, 234, 0.15);" />
        </div>

        <!-- Right Column: The Narrative -->
        <!-- Base text color updated to the readable off-white -->
        <div style="flex: 2 1 400px; font-size: 1.15rem; color: var(--text-main);">
            
            <!-- Subheader updated to burnt orange -->
            <h2 style="color: var(--burnt-orange); margin-bottom: 1rem;">
                Built for the trades, by the trades.
            </h2>
            
            <p style="margin-bottom: 1.5rem;">
                I’m Zac Kimball, most people just call me Zues, and I’m the engine 
                behind Zues Digital Designs. Based out in the woods near 
                Eatonville, Washington, my mission is straightforward: I build heavy-duty, 
                reliable software for businesses that actually get their hands dirty. 
                I don't write bloated code, and I don't speak in tech-bro buzzwords. 
                Whether it's a custom dispatch portal for an HVAC crew or a streamlined 
                inventory tracker for a cabinet shop, I build digital tools that work 
                just as hard as you do.
            </p>
            
            <p style="margin-bottom: 1.5rem;">
                My background isn't sitting in a climate-controlled cubicle. 
                I’m a U.S. Marine veteran who spent years keeping military aviation 
                electronics, flight, and targeting systems mission-ready.
                After the Corps, I spent a decade answering the call as a volunteer 
                firefighter and EMT, nine years turning wrenches as a local HVAC 
                service tech, and nearly ten years programming and operating heavy 
                CNC machinery. On top of that, I built and ran my own automated vending 
                company, Sasquatch Snacks.
                Whether it's managing scheduling and patient flow for private medical 
                and dental practices, or handling logistics, material tracking, 
                and equipment deployment for dirtwork and construction crews, I know exactly 
                what it takes to keep a business breathing. I don't just understand 
                workflows; I've built them, repaired them, and lived them.            
            </p>
            
            <p style="margin-bottom: 2rem;">
                In March 2024, a catastrophic injury took me off the shop floor and out of the attics for good. 
                But instead of clocking out, I took the exact same precision, grit, and millimeter-accuracy 
                I used to command heavy machinery and weaponized it to build high-performance business software.
                Today, I’m maintaining a 4.0 GPA in Computer Science at Clover Park Technical College, 
                focusing on one thing: engineering fast, rock-solid applications that solve real-world 
                operational bottlenecks. I don't sugarcoat, I don't take shortcuts, and I don't waste 
                your time or money on over-complicated code. If you want software built by someone 
                who actually knows how a business operates, from the grease on the floor to the profit 
                on the balance sheet. Let's Talk Shop!            
            </p>

            <a asp-controller="Contact" asp-action="Index" class="btn-cta">
                Let's Talk Shop
            </a>
        </div>
        
    </div>
</div>